  <!-- Ironpass war-ram cavalry, level 31 and above (Erebor -> Gems). The three rungs below 31
       (herder 16, rider 21, goat charger 26) stay free: the branch has to be enterable.

       Why the gate starts at exactly 31: vanilla RecruitmentCampaignBehavior only promotes a
       notable's volunteer slot while Tier < MaxVolunteerTier, and TAOM's MaxVolunteerTier is 6,
       which is levels 31-35. So a slot seeded with the pooled ironpass_ram_herder climbs to
       ironpass_ram_breaker and stops there. That makes recruit_cost live for the breaker and
       inert for the two above it, which can only be reached by paying upgrade_cost or by buying
       from the Erebor emissary. The vanguard and marshal carry a recruit_cost anyway so the gate
       is already correct if either is ever pooled.

       upgrade_cost charges the PLAYER only (Patch26 hooks PartyScreenLogic), so AI lords still
       field and promote rams for free. That is deliberate: the point of the change is more rams
       in the world, not fewer. -->
  <Troop id="ironpass_ram_breaker" resource_id="gems" upgrade_cost="2" recruit_cost="10" daily_upkeep="0.1" merchant_cost="10" />
  <Troop id="ironpass_ram_vanguard" resource_id="gems" upgrade_cost="3" recruit_cost="14" daily_upkeep="0.15" merchant_cost="14" />
  <Troop id="ironpass_ram_marshal" resource_id="gems" upgrade_cost="5" recruit_cost="18" daily_upkeep="0.25" merchant_cost="18" />

  <!-- Gondor (Castar), level 41 and above (#600). Same band as the Mordor uruk and Black
       Numenorean lines: L41 upgrade 4 / upkeep 0.2, L46 5 / 0.3, and L51 6 / 0.4 extrapolated one
       rung past the Mordor top. Level 36 and below stay free so the tree stays enterable.
       upgrade_cost charges the PLAYER only (Patch26), so AI lords still promote for free. Chosen
       knowing Castar's battle base (8) is 57 percent of War Spoils' (14), so this band costs a
       Gondor player about 1.75 times the battles.

       upgrade_cost fires only on the party-screen upgrade. It does NOT cover a notable pick:
       TaomVolunteerModel seeds an EMPTY volunteer slot straight from the recruitment pools, and
       vanilla's MaxVolunteerTier cap (RecruitmentCampaignBehavior) gates only the growth of an
       occupied slot, never the seed, so a pooled elite arrives at any level. Two of these are
       pooled: the Ithilien Ranger (10 percent at Minas Tirith and both Osgiliaths in
       recruitment_pools/gondor.json, plus two clans) and the Fountain Guard (clan_empire_west_1,
       hand-written pool; also the vassal reward). Those two carry a recruit_cost equal to their
       emissary price, the pairing the Ironpass rams use, so the notable path is gated by Patch51
       and charged on OnUnitRecruited. EveryVolunteerPooledUpkeepTroop_CarriesRecruitCost pins it.
       The first eight are the Elite Emissary offers and keep their merchant_cost; the other
       eight are not offered, so no price (an unreachable offer is dead data). -->
  <Troop id="gondor_ithilien_ranger" resource_id="caster" upgrade_cost="6" recruit_cost="45" daily_upkeep="0.4" merchant_cost="45" />
